<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aghaboe</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aghaboe Abbey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aghaboe is a village in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-laois">County Laois</a>, Ireland, and the site of a monastery founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canice">Saint Canice</a> in the 6th century. It became the chief church of the kingdom of Osraige and the first seat of the diocese of Ossory, before the see moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilkenny">Kilkenny</a> in the late 12th century. Ruins of a later Dominican friary survive there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aghaboe.jpg" alt="Aghaboe" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andreas F. Borchert · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aghaboe_Priory_of_St._Canice_Nave_2010_09_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
